  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an array of strings `words` (**0-indexed**).\n\nIn one operation, pick two **distinct** indices `i` and `j`, where `words[i]` is a non-empty string, and move **any** character from `words[i]` to **any** position in `words[j]`.\n\nOutput `true` *if you can make **every** string in* `words` ***equal** using **any** number of operations*, *and* `false` *otherwise*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: words = [\"abc\",\"aabc\",\"bc\"]\nOutput: true\nExplanation: Move the first 'a' in words[1] to the front of words[2],\nto make words[1] = \"abc\" and words[2] = \"abc\".\nAll the strings are now equal to \"abc\", so return true.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: words = [\"ab\",\"a\"]\nOutput: false\nExplanation: It is impossible to make all the strings equal using the operation.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= words.length <= 100`\n* `1 <= words[i].length <= 100`\n* `words[i]` is composed of lowercase English letters.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
